# Plan: DropUI React port (`drop-ui-react`)

> Revised 2026-10-05 against commit `9d4ff1c` ("dropdown"). The first version predated the grid-layout, form-elements, theming and dropdown commits, the two ADRs and the comment rules in `CLAUDE.md`. Updated the same day for three uncommitted changes on top of that commit: control values held in `BuilderStore`, the dropdown options dialog renamed and moved into the builder feature, and themes loaded on demand.

## Context

DropUI is an Angular 22 drag & drop UI builder. The persistence plans next to this file already say the app will be ported to other frameworks as separate projects sharing one backend. This plan covers the React port.

Decisions made with the user:

- **Location:** a new sibling repo, `C:\Users\telis\Repos\drop-ui-react`. The Angular repo is not modified.
- **State:** Zustand.

Goal: feature parity with the Angular app at `9d4ff1c` plus those changes, proven by the same three test suites. The five Playwright files in `drop-ui/e2e/` (25 tests) are the acceptance contract: they are copied over and must pass without changes to their assertions.

