## Drag & drop

| CDK | dnd-kit |
|---|---|
| `CdkDropListGroup` on the shell | one `<DndContext>` in `BuilderShell`, `PointerSensor` with `activationConstraint: { distance: 5 }` |
| palette `cdkDrag` + `cdkDropListHasAnchor` + `acceptNothing` | `useDraggable` per palette item, rendered through `<DragOverlay>` so the original stays put; the palette registers no droppable |
| cell `cdkDropList` + `[cdkDropListData]` | `useDroppable({ id, data: cell })` wrapping a `<SortableContext>` of the cell's uids |
| element `cdkDrag` | `useSortable({ id: uid, data: element })` on the wrapper `<div>` |
| `(cdkDropListDropped)` → `Canvas.drop` | `onDragEnd` → pure `resolveDrop(active, over, cells)` in `canvas-drop.ts` returning `{ kind: 'add' \| 'move', cell, index }`, then `addElement` / `moveElement` |
| `.cdk-drop-list-receiving` / `-dragging` in `styles.css` | `isOver` / `isDragging` from the hooks → conditional classes, including `z-10` on the hovered cell (cells overlap their neighbours' borders) |
| `(mousedown)` / `(touchstart)` `stopPropagation()` on the menu button **and on every form control** | `onPointerDown={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}` on the same elements, shared as one `noDrag` props object |

`resolveDrop` keeps the existing rule that only canvas elements carry `paletteUid`. Drop index: over an element → that element's index in its cell; over the cell itself → end of the cell. For a same-cell reorder this matches `moveElement`'s "index counted without the element itself".

Two tests in `form-elements.e2e.ts` pin the `noDrag` behaviour from both sides: a drag that starts on the `<input>` must not move the element (and typing in it must work), while a drag that starts on the wrapper beside the control must move it.

Cross-cell insertion preview (the gap CDK shows while hovering another list) needs an `onDragOver` projection held in local state. Do it after the e2e suite is green; it is polish, not part of the contract.

