### `DroppedElement`

Six render branches, with `HOVER_OUTLINE` copied unchanged:

| Type | Renders | Test id | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `div` | `<div>` with text | `dropped-div` | |
| `span` | `<span>` with text | `dropped-span` | |
| `text-input` | `<input type="text">`, `aria-label="Text input"` | `dropped-text-input` | `text` is the placeholder; controlled: `value={element.value}`, `onChange` → `updateValue`; `noDrag` |
| `textfield` | `<textarea>`, `aria-label="Textfield"` | `dropped-textfield` | same |
| `datepicker` | `<input type="date">`, `aria-label="Datepicker"` | `dropped-datepicker` | controlled the same way; `noDrag` |
| `dropdown` | `<select>`, `aria-label="Dropdown"` | `dropped-dropdown` | one `<option>` per entry, keyed by index; controlled: `value={element.value}`, `onChange` → `updateValue`; `noDrag` |

Control values are store state, not DOM state: an element is unmounted and remounted when it changes cell, and three tests in `form-elements.e2e.ts` check that what was typed, picked or selected survives a move and a grid shrink.

Menu items are conditional: "Edit text" when `'text' in element`, "Edit options" when `element.type === 'dropdown'`, "Delete element" always. The component holds `useState<'edit-text' | 'edit-options' | 'delete' | null>` and renders the matching dialog. Handlers take the narrowed element (`TextCanvasElement | TextControlCanvasElement`, `DropdownCanvasElement`), as ADR 0002 rule 7 requires.

### `ThemePicker`

Base UI `Menu` with a `RadioGroup` whose value is the store's theme; each theme is a `RadioItem` (role `menuitemradio`, `aria-checked`). The popup carries `aria-label="Themes"`. The four-dot swatch is a small component used in the trigger and, wrapped in `data-theme={theme}`, in each row; the check icon is `invisible` unless the row is current.

The Angular component calls `menu.setActiveMenuItem(selected)` in an effect so the list opens scrolled to the current theme (`theme.e2e.ts`: "opens the theme list scrolled to the current theme", asserted with `toBeInViewport`). In React: when the menu opens, focus the checked item, or call `scrollIntoView({ block: 'nearest' })` on it from a ref. Check the Base UI `Menu` docs for a built-in way to set the initially highlighted item before writing the ref version.

### `LayoutPanel` (the one real behavioural trap)

React's `onChange` on an `<input>` is the native `input` event and fires per keystroke. The Angular code deliberately commits on native `change` so typing "12" does not pass through "1" and collapse the grid. In React: uncontrolled inputs (`defaultValue`, a `ref`), one `commit(axis, input)` on a native `change` listener attached through the ref (fallback: `onBlur` + Enter), then `show(axis, input)` writes `input.value` back from the store. `grid-layout.e2e.ts` ("applies a typed grid size once it is committed") guards this.

## Dialogs

All three become controlled Base UI `Dialog`s with `open` and `onOpenChange`; `Dialog.Title` gives the accessible name. This replaces the `open*Dialog(dialog, options): Observable` helpers and removes RxJS. Each dialog's form body is a child component that mounts only while the dialog is open, so `useState(initialValue)` resets on every open (the `linkedSignal` equivalent) without a syncing effect.

| Dialog | Props besides `open` / `onOpenChange` / `title` | Behaviour to keep |
|---|---|---|
| `ConfirmationDialog` | `description?`, `confirmLabel?` (default `'Confirm'`), `onConfirm` | Cancel has initial focus |
| `TextInputDialog` | `description?`, `value?`, `onSubmit(text)` | textbox "Text" has initial focus; Save disabled while `!text.trim()` |
| `DropdownOptionsDialog` | `description?`, `options?`, `onSubmit(options)` | see below |

`DropdownOptionsDialog` lives in the builder feature, not in `shared/`, because it edits a builder model type. It is a dynamic list of rows:

- State: `useState<Row[]>` where `Row = { id, text, value }`. The `id` (`crypto.randomUUID()`) exists only as the React `key`: index keys would move typed values and focus to the wrong row after a delete. Rows are stripped back to `{ text, value }` on submit, the same job `copyOption` does today.
- Starts with the given options, or one blank row when there are none.
- `invalid = rows.some((row) => !row.text.trim() || !row.value.trim())`; Save is disabled while invalid, and submit is a no-op.
- "Add option" appends a blank row and focuses its text input. "Delete option N" removes the row and focuses the previous row's text input, so focus does not fall out of the dialog. The first row's delete button is disabled.
- Labels: "Option N text", "Option N value", "Delete option N" (one-based).
- Never mutates the `options` prop (the spec passes frozen arrays).

## Tests

- `vitest.config.ts` with two projects: `unit` (`src/**/*.spec.ts`, jsdom) and `components` (`src/**/*.test.tsx`, Chromium via `@vitest/browser-playwright`), reusing the two setup files.
- npm scripts keep the same names so the commands do not change: `test` → `vitest --project unit`, `test:components` → `vitest --project components`, `e2e` → `playwright test`.
- Store specs: `builder-store.spec.ts` and `theme-store.spec.ts` replace `TestBed.inject(...)` with the factories and signal reads with `store.getState()` / `selectCells(...)`. `createThemeStore` takes a detached document so the spec can seed `data-theme` and assert the attribute write and the appended stylesheet link.
- Component class-logic specs become pure-function specs: `canvas.spec.ts` → `canvas-drop.spec.ts` for `resolveDrop`; the `dropped-element.spec.ts` hover-outline cases → the `HOVER_OUTLINE` mapping. Spec cases that drove a dialog's form model or `dialogRef.close` directly (`dropdown-options-dialog.spec.ts`, `text-input-dialog.spec.ts`, `confirmation-dialog.spec.ts`, the rest of `dropped-element.spec.ts`, `layout-panel.spec.ts`) move to the component's `*.test.tsx` as observable behaviour, asserting on the `onSubmit` / `onConfirm` callback prop, which the testing guide already allows for parent-supplied handlers. The `open*Dialog` helper specs have nothing to port.
- Component tests: `src/test/render-with-stores.tsx` wraps `render` in both store providers (and `DndContext` where needed) with preset state. Assertions in the existing `*.test.ts` files port with only the mount helper changed. Fixtures are built per element kind, never by spreading one kind into another (ADR 0002, "Costs").
- E2E: copy the five files. `playwright.config.ts` is the same except `webServer.command: 'npm run dev'` and port **5173** (not 4200), so `reuseExistingServer` can never attach to a running Angular dev server.
- Tests carry no comments, per `CLAUDE.md`.

